Simplify Deployments with AWS Elastic Beanstalk 🚀
Topic: Deploy Full-Stack Applications in Minutes with AWS Elastic Beanstalk

On Day 12 of my hashtag#AWSChallenge, I explored Elastic Beanstalk – one of the easiest ways to deploy and manage applications in the AWS Cloud, without worrying about infrastructure setup.

🔍 What is Elastic Beanstalk?
Elastic Beanstalk is a Platform as a Service (PaaS) that automates:

Environment provisioning

Load balancing

Auto scaling

Monitoring

Application updates

All you need to do is upload your code, and Elastic Beanstalk handles the rest!

✅ Supported Languages & Platforms:
Node.js, Python, Java, .NET, Go

Docker (single & multi-container)

PHP, Ruby, Tomcat

Static file hosting with Nginx or Apache

🔧 What I Did:
Created a simple Node.js app

Deployed it using Elastic Beanstalk CLI (eb init, eb create, eb deploy)

Monitored logs, health status, and events via AWS Console

Integrated Auto Scaling and load balancing out-of-the-box!

🧠 Key Benefits:
Managed infrastructure – you focus only on code

Built-in monitoring – integrated with CloudWatch

Version control – deploy, rollback, and monitor every version

CI/CD Friendly – works great with GitHub actions or CodePipeline

🛠 Bonus Tip:
You can use .ebextensions to customize EC2, install software, or manage config files during deployment. Super handy for advanced setups!

💡 Use Case:
Host web applications, REST APIs, or background services with minimal ops overhead and maximum reliability using AWS-native PaaS.
